<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Galicia</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Galicia is a historical region in east-central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a>, now divided between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poland">Poland</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ukraine">Ukraine</a>. Annexed by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austria">Austria</a> in the first partition of Poland, it became a crown land of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austro-hungarian-empire">Austro-Hungarian Empire</a> with Polish autonomy, and it was the scene of heavy fighting and great Austro-Hungarian losses in 1914.</p></div>
